OL,3,GNEWSA'Long, hard road' from skydive
OL,4,Ainjury to Ironman
OL,5,
OL,6,FA former Royal Marine commando has
OL,7,Fdescribed his "single-minded mental
OL,8,Fapproach" in competing in one of the
OL,9,Fworld's toughest Ironman challenges,
OL,10,Fthree years after surgery following a
OL,11,Fskydive accident.
OL,13,FMichael Oakes, 50, from Andover,
OL,14,FHampshire, was told he may never walk
OL,15,Fagain after the accident at Netheravon,
OL,16,FWiltshire, in 2023.
OL,18,FHe is taking part in the Ironman World
OL,19,FChampionship in Kailua-Kona, Hawaii,
OL,20,Finvolving a 2.4-mile swim, 112-mile
OL,21,Fcycle and 26.2-mile marathon.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
